<HelpTab>
    <HelpSection Title="Reporting a message">
        <ol>
            <li>Open the … menu on the message and select <strong>Report</strong>.</li>
            <li>Choose what's wrong with it: <strong>Harassment or bullying</strong>, <strong>Offensive or
                inappropriate</strong>, <strong>Spam</strong> or <strong>Something else</strong>.</li>
            <li>Add anything else your manager should know, then select <strong>Report</strong>.</li>
        </ol>
        <FluentText>
            Your managers see that message only, not the rest of the conversation, and the person isn't told who
            reported it. You're told when a manager has reviewed it. In a direct message you can also tick
            <strong>Also block</strong> to stop them messaging you.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Blocking someone">
        <FluentText>
            In a direct message, open the ⋮ menu and select <strong>Block</strong>. Neither of you can message the other,
            and they aren't told. You'll still see each other in groups. Unblock them from the same menu.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="If you can't post">
        <ul>
            <li>"Only managers can post here at the moment": the channel is read-only for now, but you can still read it.</li>
            <li>"You can't post in chat until …": a manager has paused your posting after a report. You can still read
                messages.</li>
        </ul>
    </HelpSection>
</HelpTab>
